  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Aviation Security Equipment Testing and Evaluation Program, through Engineering and Information Technologies Inc.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This Technical Assistance (TA) grant will assist the Airports Authority of India (AAI) and India&apos;s Bureau of Cival Aviation Security (BCAS) to establish an Aviation Security Equipment Testing and Evaluation Program (ASETEP). The ASETEP will include development of clear standards, specifications and testing prcedures that align with international best practices for three types of aviation security equipment that scan carry-on luggage, checked baggage and passengers. USTDA is amending the Technical Assistance grant to Airports Authority of India for the Aviation Security Equipment Testing and Evaluation Program (USTDA Activity No.: 2014-31021A). This amendment will revise the Contractor&apos;s requirements to complete Task 12 of the Terms of Reference.</narrative>
  </description>
